{"metadata":{"abstractText":"In our continuing search for novel antiplatelet agents, 4-alkoxy derivatives of 2-phenylquinoline as well as related compounds were prepared. Through biological screening, a preliminary structure antiplatelet activity relationship was established. Compounds 5-ethyl-4-methoxy-2-phenylquinoline (8), 4-ethoxy-5-ethyl-2-phenylquinoline (9), 4-ethoxycarbonylmethoxy-5-ethyl-2-phenylquinoline (10), 4-ethoxycarbonylbutoxy-5-ethyl-2-phenylquinoline (12) and 5-ethyl-4-(N-ethylcarboxido)methoxy-2-phenylquinoline (17) all demonstrated potent antiplatelet activity. Among them, compound 8 was the most potent with an IC50 value of 0.08 microM and was about 3-fold more active than indomethacin. The mechanism of antiplatelet action of 8 is possibly through its inhibition on cyclooxygenase or thromboxane synthetase.","affiliation":"Graduate Institute of Pharmaceutical Chemistry, China Medical College, Taichung, Taiwan.","authMan":"N","authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9719-7334"}]},"authorList":{"author":[{"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Graduate Institute of Pharmaceutical Chemistry, China Medical College, Taichung, Taiwan."}]},"firstName":"T C","fullName":"Ko TC","initials":"TC","lastName":"Ko"},{"firstName":"M J","fullName":"Hour MJ","initials":"MJ","lastName":"Hour"},{"firstName":"J C","fullName":"Lien JC","initials":"JC","lastName":"Lien"},{"authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9719-7334"},"firstName":"C M","fullName":"Teng CM","initials":"CM","lastName":"Teng"},{"firstName":"K H","fullName":"Lee KH","initials":"KH","lastName":"Lee"},{"firstName":"S C","fullName":"Kuo SC","initials":"SC","lastName":"Kuo"},{"firstName":"L J","fullName":"Huang LJ","initials":"LJ","lastName":"Huang"}]},"authorString":"Ko TC, Hour MJ, Lien JC, Teng CM, Lee KH, Kuo SC, Huang LJ.","chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Collagen","registryNumber":"9007-34-5"},{"name":"Quinolines","registryNumber":"0"},{"